.TH SHEETVIEW 2
.SH NAME
sheetview \- a document's sheets in a column, on an image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "docengine.m";
include "docreg.m";
include "sheetview.m";
sheetview := load Sheetview Sheetview->PATH;

init:  fn(d: ref Draw->Display);
new:   fn(k: ref Docreg->Kind, name: string, c: chan of ref Ev): ref View;

View: adt {
	dst:    ref Draw->Image;   # set by the caller
	r:      Draw->Rect;
	bg, mark: ref Draw->Image;
	font:   ref Draw->Font;
	style:  ref Docengine->Style;
	eng:    Docengine;         # the document
	h:      int;
	scale, rot, fit: int;      # the view
	org:    Draw->Point;
	sizes:  array of Draw->Point;
	...
	open:     fn(v: self ref View, data: array of byte, name: string);
	browse:   fn(v: self ref View, url: string): string;
	close:    fn(v: self ref View);
	handle:   fn(v: self ref View, e: ref Ev): ref Note;
	draw:     fn(v: self ref View);
	layout:   fn(v: self ref View);
	scroll:   fn(v: self ref View, dy: int);
	pan:      fn(v: self ref View, org: Draw->Point);
	zoom:     fn(v: self ref View, scale: int);
	setfit:   fn(v: self ref View, fit: int);
	rotate:   fn(v: self ref View, quarters: int);
	gotosheet: fn(v: self ref View, n: int);
	sheetat:  fn(v: self ref View, y: int): int;
	sheetrect: fn(v: self ref View, n: int): Draw->Rect;
	size:     fn(v: self ref View, n: int): Draw->Point;
	at:       fn(v: self ref View, p: Draw->Point): (int, Draw->Point);
	wordof:   fn(v: self ref View, n: int, p: Draw->Point): (string, Draw->Rect, int);
	select:   fn(v: self ref View, n: int, word: string, r: Draw->Rect);
	find:     fn(v: self ref View, s: string): string;
	foundon:  fn(v: self ref View, n: int): list of Draw->Rect;
	result:   fn(v: self ref View, res: string): ref Note;
	command:  fn(v: self ref View, cmd, arg: string): (int, string);
	commands: fn(v: self ref View): list of string;
};
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sheetview
is the view every program that shows documents shares: Xenith's
windows and
.IR page (1).
A document is held by its engine
.RI ( docengine (2))
as a column of sheets; the view stacks them, a gap between, and draws
the part at
.I org
into the rectangle
.I r
of the image
.IR dst :
fitted to its width
.RB ( Fitwidth ,
a PDF), a whole sheet in view
.RB ( Fitpage ,
a picture), at a scale
.RB ( Fitnone ),
or, for a flowing document (Markdown, HTML, a page browsed), set to
its width in
.IR style .
.PP
.I New
makes a view of a document of kind
.I k
named
.IR name ;
.I open
opens it from
.I data
(or, nil, the file or URL named),
.I browse
as a web page.  The engine is loaded and the document opened off the
caller's thread, and what is done off it comes back as an
.B Ev
on
.IR c :
.B Opened
(or not), a binary document's
.B Text
(read after it is shown),
a sheet
.B Painted
at a scale, an engine's own
.B Engine
event.  The caller hands each to
.I handle
on its own thread and acts on the
.B Note
returned:
.B Opened
(draw it),
.BI Failed( err ) ,
.BI Text( text ) ,
.BI Loaded( name ", " text )
(a page browsed loaded),
.BI Error( err )
or
.BR Redraw .
Nothing in the view calls the caller, and only
.I draw
draws; the calls that move the view
.RI ( scroll ,
.IR pan ,
.IR zoom ,
.IR setfit ,
.IR rotate ,
.IR gotosheet ,
.IR find )
change it, for the caller to draw when it shows it.
.PP
A sheet an engine paints sharp at any scale is painted at the view's,
by a proc of its own, and kept while it is in view or is the next the
way the view last moved
.RI ( dir );
until it arrives, a painting at another scale is shown scaled.
A flowing document at scale 100 is painted off
.I dst
into a band of the view and half a view above and below
.RI ( band ,
.IR bandr ):
a scroll within it is a copy, and one past it paints only the strip it
exposes.
.I Result
and anything that lays the document out again drop the band.
The view is never filled before its sheets are drawn, only the gaps
round them.
.I Rotate
turns the sheets by quarter turns: a sheet is turned once, as it is
painted;
.I size
gives a sheet's size turned, and
.I at
the sheet and the engine's point under a point of
.IR dst .
.I Layout
lays the column out again for
.IR r ,
the scale and the style as they are, keeping the sheet at the top of
the view and the place in it.
.PP
.I Wordof
is the word the engine drew at a point,
.I select
marks one,
.I find
finds the sheets whose text has a string (marked on them as they are
drawn) and brings the first into view,
.I foundon
gives where on a sheet.
.I Command
does
.BR Zoom+ ,
.BR Zoom- ,
.BI Zoom " n" ,
.BR Fit " [" page ],
.BI Page " n" ,
.BR NextPage ,
.B PrevPage
and the engine's own;
.I commands
lists them.
.I Result
does what an engine's answer to a click or a key asks.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/sheetview.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR page (1),
.IR docengine (2),
.B docs/xenith-documents.md
